# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Geniro runtime data (generated per-project, git-ignored by default)
# Includes transient skill state: .geniro/state/<skill>/<slug>/state.md,
# .geniro/planning/<task-dir>/state.md, .geniro/knowledge/learnings.jsonl
# `.geniro/*` (asterisk form) is required so the !-negations below take effect.
.geniro/*
!.geniro/
!.geniro/workflow/
!.geniro/workflow/**
!.geniro/instructions/
!.geniro/instructions/**
!.geniro/actions/
!.geniro/actions/**

# Claude Code agent / runtime artifacts (worktrees created by Agent + EnterWorktree
# can leave gitlink pointers if accidentally staged — exclude the directory entirely).
.claude/worktrees/

# Node (if any tooling is added)
node_modules/

# Evals — raw per-trial transcripts/outputs are local-only; the framework,
# benchmarks, and the runs.jsonl ledger ARE committed.

# design/scratch/ — local-only working area for ALL skill-/maintainer-generated
# design docs: plans, research, fix-pass progress, AND audit reports. Nothing here
# is committed. /audit-plugin writes its reports here, and a same-machine rerun can
# still read them; a fresh clone simply starts without them.
#
# Nothing carries a decision forward from one audit round to the next, by design:
# a finding worth remembering becomes a hard check under tests/authoring/, which
# CI enforces and which stops firing once the violation is gone.
design/scratch/
.codegraph
evals/loop/runs/
evals/loop/cache/
# Raw sweep output of any eval suite — prompts, model responses, per-run scores
evals/suites/*/runs/
# Machine-local mappings that keep committed content free of repo names/paths
evals/loop/repos.local.json
.claude/skills/find-threads/roots.local
# Benchmark tasks mined from a PRIVATE repository. Their ground truth is that
# repo's real file paths and identifiers, and it cannot be anonymized without
# breaking what it measures — a rubric matches by real path against a tree
# staged from that repo, so a renamed path matches nothing. This repository is
# public, so those tasks live here, beside repos.local.json, and never in git.
evals/loop/modules/*/benchmarks.local/
